[b]Every hit rolls. Every blow costs.[/b] Damage that is never quite the same twice, and a stamina bar — [b]Athletics[/b] — that decides who is still fresh when the lines meet.

Looking for a [b]stamina[/b] or [b]fatigue[/b] mod, or [b]random damage[/b]? This is one.

[h1]What it does[/h1]
[list]
[*][b]±50% damage[/b] — every hit that lands, melee or ranged, rolls anew: a 50-damage blow lands for anything from 25 to 75. Blocked blows, falls and doors stay vanilla.
[*][b]The Athletics bar[/b] — every fighter's stamina, as big as his [b]Athletics skill[/b] (never under 50). Every blow costs 10 points: a swing, a thrust, a shot or a throw. Kicks and shield bashes are free.
[*][b]Heroes pay less[/b] — lords, companions and you pay ×0.75 a blow, a party leader ×0.75 again. A big-skill hero has a big bar: the battle leans on its heroes.
[*][b]Full strength in the top quarter[/b] — above the white mark (75% of the bar) a fighter is at his best. Below it his lucky hits, his attack rate and his run speed fade in a straight line, down to one attack where he used to make five, and a 30% run, when it is empty. Blocking is never slowed; horses keep their speed.
[*][b]Wounds cap the bar[/b] — at half health, half a bar. A badly hurt man never gets back to full strength.
[*][b]Rest to refill[/b] — one minute standing or walking, from empty to full; twice that running flat out.
[*][b]Tired men step back[/b] — after a swing, a tired soldier on foot may step back out of the press, facing his enemy with his guard up, and rejoin his line a moment later. The more tired, the more often. The fresh take the blows. Field battles only.
[*][b]Your Athletics bar[/b] — under your health bar: the number, the white mark, green at full strength, then blue, yellow, orange and red as you tire; the part your wounds hold shown dark.
[*][b]The orders-menu strip[/b] — open the orders menu and each formation card shows its men's average Athletics with its spread, and their average health ([i]72% ± 8 · HP 81%[/i]).
[/list]

[h1]Every number is yours[/h1]
[list]
[*]In the [url=https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=2859238197]Mod Configuration Menu (MCM)[/url] if you have it — [b]optional[/b]: the mod runs without it.
[*]Or in a plain config file, with an explanation beside every value: [i]Documents\Mount and Blade II Bannerlord\Configs\TraxCombatEnhancements\config.json[/i]
[*]Changes in MCM apply at once, even mid-battle. Nothing ever needs a restart.
[*][b]A master switch[/b] turns the whole mod off, even mid-battle: the fight is pure vanilla, so you can play the same battle both ways and compare.
[/list]

[h1]Compatibility[/h1]
[list]
[*][b]NOT compatible with Realistic Battle Mod (RBM)[/b] — it has its own stamina and posture. Use one or the other; the mod warns you at the main menu if it sees RBM.
[*]Other mods that change damage or attack speed may stack with this one.
[*][b]Safe to add or remove mid-campaign[/b] — it lives inside battles and writes nothing to your save.
[*]Game [b]v1.4.8[/b], singleplayer: campaign and custom battles. No Harmony patches.
[*]Built to sit beside [b]RTS Camera[/b] (its order menu too) and [b]War Sails[/b] (no step backs on deck).
[/list]

[h1]First release — be gentle, and tell me[/h1]
This is the first release. Every part was built and tested against the game's own code, but it has not been played across many campaigns yet. Please tell me if:
[list]
[*]tired men turn their backs or get stuck when they step back — until it is fixed, switch off [i]Tired fighters step back[/i];
[*]the orders-menu strip does not line up with the formation cards at your resolution or UI scale (it falls back to a small panel);
[*]anything misbehaves beside RTS Camera or War Sails;
[*]the balance feels off — the numbers are a first guess, and they will be tuned.
[/list]
The mod keeps a log beside its config file, [i]trax_combat.log[/i], with a summary of every battle. Attaching it to a report helps a lot.

[h1]Feedback[/h1]
Bugs and ideas: [url=https://github.com/TraxData313/trax_combat_enhancements/issues]GitHub issues[/url], or the comments below. The source is on [url=https://github.com/TraxData313/trax_combat_enhancements]GitHub[/url] — public domain (The Unlicense).
